## Example idea (informal)

> This is NOT a final model, just a flavor.

- Base concept:  
  - \((\text{proton}, \text{electron}, \text{neutron})\) as structural carriers  
- Build up:
  - atom → molecule → material  
- For each level:
  - define a **finite state set** (≤ 128)  
  - define **transitions** (what changes, why, under which conditions)

---

## How to contribute

1. **Open an issue** with the label `material-proposal`
2. Provide:
   - **Name of material** (DE/EN)  
   - **Safety**: short note why it is non-dangerous in this context  
   - **State model**:
     - number of states (≤ 128)  
     - short description of each state or state class  
   - **Optional**: references (papers, textbooks, reputable sources)
3. Or create a **pull request** with:
   - a new `.md` file under `materials/`  
   - your proposed model in clear, simple language

---

## Why this matters

This repo is meant to be:

- a **didactic bridge** between real science and discrete system models  
- a **playground** for finite-state thinking on real, non-dangerous matter  
- a **transparent base** for later, more complex system work (4ALL, NoN, etc.)

No hype.  
No Babo.  
Just **clean models, clear language, shared attention**.

